In article <25SEP199303030716@venus.tamu.edu>, ebb7683@venus.tamu.edu (Ed Blackman) writes:

>Actually, that brings up a good question.  When you do the bit with the
>bell book and candle, it levels the dungeon in a big circle around you,
>centered on the vibrating square.  In all of the times that I've played 
>that far, I've never had that circle run partially off screen... it was
>always whole.  If that always holds true, you could cut a big chunk off
>of the area you have to search by always staying a distance away from the 
>nearest wall that is greater than or equal to the radius of the circle.
>
>Would someone with the source take a look at how the placement of the
>VS is determined to see if it has any such restrictions?

It sure does:

Here's the code where it picks a spot for the vibrating square:
                place_lregion(0,0,0,0, 30, 0, 46, ROWNO, UP, (d_level *)0);
                do {
                        if(xupstair < 30)
                                x = rn1(COLNO-16-xupstair, xupstair+7);
                        else
                                x = rn1(xupstair-16, 9);
                        y = rn1(7, 8);
                } while((levl[x][y].typ != CORR && levl[x][y].typ != ROOM)
                        || occupied(x,y));
                inv_pos.x = x;
                inv_pos.y = y;

Let's try to figure this mess out.  
  - The first line places the upstairs anywhere on the screen except for 
    between columns 30 and 46 (although why they used UP instead of 
    LR_UPSTAIR is beyond me).
  - Next, if the stairs are on the left side of the screen, it places the
    square between at least 7 squares right of the upstairs, and at least
    9 squares from the right edge.
  - Otherwise, if the stairs are on the right side of the screen, it places
    the square between row 9 and 7 squares to the left of the upstairs.
  - The y position is always between 8 and 15.

So, assuming stairs are on the left side, the search area is like this:

+------------------------------------------------+
|                                                |
|            XXXXXXXX  row 8 XXXXXXXXXXX         |
|            XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX         |
|            XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX         |
|   >(7 cols)XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX (9 cols)|
|            XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX         |
|            XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX         |
|            XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX         |
|            XXXXXXXX  row 15 XXXXXXXXXX         |
|                                                |
|                                                |
|                                                |
|                                                |
